## 6. ACCESS CONTROL LOGIC

The access control pattern used throughout:
```php
private function isAdmin(): bool {
    return $this->getUser()->getRole() === 'ADMIN';
}
```

- **ADMIN**: sees all projects, all activities, can edit/delete any
- **HR**: sees only their own projects (where `projectManager = currentUser`), sees only activities linked to their projects, can only assign activities to their own projects' candidates
- **CANDIDATE (front-office)**: sees only their own assigned activities via `ActivityController`

When checking project ownership for HR:
```php
if (!$this->isAdmin() && $project->getProjectManagerId() !== $this->getUser()->getId()) {
    throw $this->createAccessDeniedException();
}
```

